👉 A data type defines the type of data a variable can store.
👉 It also determines the amount of memory allocated.
👉 Primary data types in C are:
  👉 int → Whole numbers
  👉 float → Decimal numbers
  👉 double → High-precision decimal numbers
  👉 char → Single characters
👉 Different data types use different format specifiers in printf().
👉 Choosing the correct data type improves memory usage and program efficiency.



